  "detail": null,
  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07). All 7 patients reviewed. Every change has a progress note with cited sources.\n\n- pt-0061 Irene Castellano: apixaban raised from 2.5 to 5 mg BID (mr-t0001). Age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02, so no dose criteria met. Her itraconazole course ended 08/14 (ID letter, doc-61002).\n- pt-0003 Frank Delgado: rivaroxaban first cut from 20 to 15 mg on St. Brigid SCr 160 µmol/L. The lab then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL), giving CrCl 59.9. Order set back to 20 mg daily (mr-t0011), so his dose is unchanged overall.\n- pt-0041 Raymond Duquette: apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0005). No criteria met, but he has an active itraconazole order.\n- pt-0062 Norman Fairweather: no change, stays on apixaban 5 mg BID. Only the age criterion (82) is met. A new ED SCr of 150 µmol/L (10/21) was replaced by 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) the next day.\n- pt-0038 Eugene Moravec: rivaroxaban raised from 15 to 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). CrCl is 56.1 on actual weight (96 kg, SCr 1.45). The May reduction used ideal body weight, which the policy doesn't allow. His portal message reporting 185 lb on his home scale is patient-reported, not measured, so the dose stays at 20 mg.\n- pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino: first left at 20 mg (CrCl 59.2). A new SCr of 1.25 (10/22) came in, giving CrCl 43.6, so rivaroxaban was lowered to 15 mg daily (mr-t0012).\n- pt-0002 Harold Vance: first raised from 2.5 to 5 mg BID (only the age criterion met; 64.9 kg, SCr 1.21). A St. Brigid dermatology letter then arrived saying itraconazole was started 10/22, so the order was set to 2.5 mg BID (mr-t0013). He stays on 2.5 mg.\n\nPolicy says not to change other medications, so none were changed, itraconazole included. The 5 items that arrived during the review are completed with notes. Earlier inbox items for other patients were not touched.\n\nFollow-up: recheck the apixaban dose for pt-0041 and pt-0002 when their 12-week itraconazole courses end. Get a clinic-measured weight for pt-0038 at his next visit.",
  "resumed": false,
